  "summary": "The Rugby 610 is a single-button self-levelling horizontal laser: one switch for on and off, self-levelling within 5 degrees, and nothing to configure. It is the simplest rotating laser Leica builds, and it is built to be used by crews who do not want to read a manual.\n\nAccuracy is +/- 2.2 mm at 30 m, the working diameter reaches 800 m with a Rod Eye 120 receiver and 1,100 m with the Rod Eye 140 or 160, and the battery runs up to 120 hours on Li-ion. IP67 with or without the battery fitted.\n\nIt covers the everyday work: levelling and aligning formwork, pads, and footings, transferring reference heights, and checking grade during a pour.",
